module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.native_infer_accepts_only_bool_and_int_match_scrutinees

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data native_infer_accepts_only_bool_and_int_match_scrutinees: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "native_infer_accepts_only_bool_and_int_match_scrutinees" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**the native v2 front end's infer accepts only Bool and Int match scrutinees -- a `match` whose scrutinee's type is a variant (coproduct) refuses its module at prepare with infer_match_scrutinee_not_bool, so variant-field lowering is never reached on the native route** (INVALID STATE: every claim body that would observe variant-field lowering must first match over a variant, and the emitted infer has no path for that scrutinee).",
    "RECEIPT (2026-10-02, eager-cat-664, head 17fccbf3f62): the first native run over a variant-match test module -- `gunbc test '//v2/test/claim/variant_field_native_binding:all'` with GITHUB_SHA set (seed emit of src/v2/compiler/00_compile.dag, 225 files, closure ae6fb52183d56945c0dedad90047279110c416c3f7ea5dcb6b5a10724ab7cff6; emitted crate built clean under -D warnings, rustc 1.98.1 aarch64; the phase's own discriminating red EMIT_COMPILE_MUTATION_PROBE established; malformed control observed). target/v2-native-lane/driver-rows.jsonl records all four identities of v2.test.claim.variant_field_native_binding (vfb_positional_construction_and_match_round_trip_field_zero, vfb_positional_round_trip_through_a_call_holds, vfb_named_construction_and_match_round_trip_holds, vfb_named_arm_of_a_positional_value_stays_unmatched) as NativeTestRefused at NativeTestStagePrepare, each carrying head reason infer_grounding_not_derived at the claim's own match spine with tail entries inhabitance_undecidable_argument_type_not_derived and infer_match_scrutinee_not_bool. The gate is v2.compiler.04_infer's infer_match_bool: where the scrutinee's resolved type is neither infer_branch_type_is_bool nor infer_branch_type_is_int, it rejects the match with infer_match_scrutinee_not_bool_diagnostic. The same four claims are GREEN on the interpreted floor (gunbc run --claim-run, pool 7223 modules, exit 0).",
    "HARM, AND THE FLOOR BLINDNESS IS PART OF THE FINDING: the interpreted floor never runs the native front end's infer over test modules -- it evaluates them directly -- so a claim module can be green on the floor and refused on the native route with no floor signal; the floor's green is not evidence about the native infer frontier, and this class was found only by executing the route.",
    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS. Not match_on_a_call_scrutinee_refused_as_arm_navigation (that refusal is at normalize on the interpreted route because the scrutinee is a CALL expression; here the scrutinee's TYPE -- a variant -- is what the infer gate rejects, on the native route, at prepare). Not the v2 body-lowering match rows (match_arms_after_the_second_are_dropped_at_v2_body_lowering and siblings): the refusal precedes body lowering. Not gunbc.rung_drop.variant_fields_unlowered_on_the_native_route, which records the frontier this refusal BLOCKS; this row records the refusal itself, one class per row.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable -- typed and loud at prepare, per-identity rows persisted in driver-rows.jsonl with the reason set.",
    "RECEIPT (2026-10-05, clever-bat-68, PR #13210, head 00cead6b3b): the prepare refusal is GONE. `gunbc test '//v2/test/claim/variant_field_native_binding:all'` with GITHUB_SHA set derives universe=4 population=4 file_refusals=0 -- the same enrolled label that recorded the four NativeTestRefused rows at head 17fccbf3f62 now selects all four identities with no file refusal, because v2.compiler.04_infer's infer accepts variant scrutinees and grounds arm binders from the declaring coproduct's payloads (the construct read types by the variant's declaring path, which symbol_index_declaring_path_of answers at the alias because symbol_index_fill_containment_node files the alias as a BINDING to its declaring path (the receipt a_binding_position_recorded_as_a_declaring_identity's named repair, landed in this PR; the earlier carrier parallel map is retired); the per-tag coverage count is replaced by the single inhabitance relation's PositionMatchCoverage position, failing closed with infer_match_coverage_undecidable when the relation cannot decide). The variant-scrutinee discriminating evidence is the probe module v2.test.claim.variant_field_infer_probe: the located refusal reds (two-arm mismatch, projection, nullary, construction, call-result scrutinee underived) and the green controls beside them (construct read names the variant, construct read carrier is the declaring coproduct, partial match refuses as not covering the carrier, call-result arm binder types from its concrete payload field, arrow fixture resolves and names its variant, partial fixture still mints its variant row), each red without the change. The generic-payload controls (bare formal, compound Box<T>, arrow fn(Int)->T) are DEFERRED, not enrolled: their honest own-frame fixture walks measure 7-10x the new-witness enrolment ceiling -- readings and the A/B trigger recorded in gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_generic_variant_construct_infer_walk_costs_about_seven_times_the_new_witness_ceiling; the resolve-side gate (03_resolve resolve_payload_field_type_holds_declaring_formal) now leaves formal-typed payload binders untyped rather than minting the formal, so the deferred controls arrive at an honest underived shape (decode receipt: the generic fixture's arm fact moved from infer_match_arm_type_mismatch to the underived marker at this head). NOT YET THE RETIREMENT TRIGGER: the route's verdict layer recorded no verdicts for the selection on this run (admission refused: positive_population_empty, required_native_pass_regressed, unattributed_exclusions_present -- the same three names recorded-not-chased on the main lane), so no NativeTestPassed rows exist beside the floor green; this row stays open until those rows land, and the retirement is NOT claimed here.",
    "CEILING: structurally guaranteed. The gate names its own frontier; a coproduct's Disj already carries each alternative's payload (v2.compiler.04_infer's infer_sum_nullary_payload_edge reads a nullary alternative as a childless Conj beside its payload-bearing Named arms), so arm typing from variant payloads is decidable.",
    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, naming the capability: variant-scrutinee match infer plus payload binder grounding in the emitted front end -- a match whose scrutinee's type is a coproduct accepts at prepare, arm binders ground from the alternative's payload fields, and the four vfb_* round-trip identities pass native prepare (NativeTestPassed rows beside the floor green).",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
